{"title":"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Euler&#39;s_Totient_+_CRT)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Euler's Totient + CRT)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(exponent_pattern)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (exponent pattern)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the tens digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a23794223519404dbf82b5f6e148ffcf2a272a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2016}-2017?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32ef4b4f196baf40edb38b6d1d9c8fbdcea89e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5cbd326de28154006f0382373b7d5d3a3e8de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^n\\equiv 15^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb8f7e86a67710596d7456d77284dab79cdffe10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/231ca6446f84b84dbbc19f7c286788763e2f268a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. (Check for yourself).  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is even, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/1755b00aa4945ab7bd2b75310246956916908f5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2016} \\equiv 25\\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9e62b30aa6bf257e35dadd52184a892703495b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2016}-2017 \\equiv 25 - 17 \\equiv \\underline{0}8\\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"336\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b85b17968b605cf6be4293b97638f79dd4006c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\boxed{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a very similar fashion, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd53ce1e2e7a16714f88d19a4fd2d4f921af11bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2016} \\equiv 15^{2016} \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"19\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876f1b262c58e2e253b0a68dd1231915c0f488bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225^{1008}$\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. Next, since every power (greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) of every number ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> will end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> (which can easily be verified), we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611726a945b6474515162cba97ee449c4333688a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225^{1008} \\equiv 25 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />. (In this way, we don't have to worry about the exponent very much.) Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e9a5bf10cb4e377a400a3ab5743389ad548ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017 \\equiv 17 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce8c31442f2f4177622f14f12bbafb0024382d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2016}-2017 \\equiv 25-17 \\equiv 08 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"336\" height=\"19\" />, as above.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Euler.27s_Totient_.2B_CRT.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Euler's_Totient_+_CRT)\">Solution 3 (Euler's Totient + CRT)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Euler&#39;s Totient + CRT)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c7b79d1b6073ddc695b0b857ad8aedb3eb3f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2000} \\equiv 15^{2000} \\equiv 15^{40} \\equiv 15^{\\varphi(100)} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"398\" height=\"23\" />. Therefore, we must find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c346b05705311c20750dbedcecdf7de3be94f86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{16} \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />. Note that we then wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c389ccc86a6dde30e7a7f1ff525af52273a7cd8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{16} \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/13506185fc537a924cc890f7665b8a6ab5834351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{16} \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" />. Obviously the latter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87a3c21d7658b70874fee27ee53355244f5d6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> and we see the former is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/72765bcd3384919aafaff1caa713cd82295a7b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{16} \\pmod{4} \\equiv 3^{2} \\pmod{4} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"21\" />. Note that then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9b9d7ec51d25806302c11b943c6d997d8f6242.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\pmod{4}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155bcc1123335373e9b6f031ae7a2edd7f918d34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 \\pmod{25}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\nIn which either through CRT or inspection we see 25 satisfies this so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/203f06919dcf938b8775265cc4729c584dcb77ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{16} \\equiv 25 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e017b1b25afdb4249c49bfa354fd628597a4e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25-17 \\pmod{100} \\equiv 08 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"20\" />, so the tens digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a4ccfb0098b8620892ab28beee6fbc5782014b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28exponent_pattern.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(exponent_pattern)\">Solution 4 (exponent pattern)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (exponent pattern)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we only need the tens digits, we only need to care about the multiplication of tens and ones. (If you want to use mathematical terms then we only need to look at the exponents in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c1c91d8abd02119ce4afea01d6ba2b807a63ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$mod 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />.) We will use the \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/1165e91155febc4bc88785c5504eb52efe4f8c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"8\" />\" sign to denote congruence in modulus, basically taking the last two digits and ignoring everything else.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fd818661e17c795c8fceb8a2202b124962322b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} 15^{1}\\equiv15 \\\\ 15^{2}\\equiv25 \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"43\" />\nFrom here we only need to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8effed83b7badf16efcd78840d23d8d1ddc54c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\cdot25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> and we can ignore the hundreds digits.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e62bb97c3e25642c8506c77b50110c2b8e6da8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} 15^{3}\\equiv75 \\\\ 15^{4}\\equiv25 \\\\ 15^{5}\\equiv75 \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"70\" />\nNotice that for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee5f5346e45a669b3e3289403967d5cc5ddf200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/2/182f3c217d5f603e9fa91d1c0b59290757faf0e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{x}\\equiv25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c5731576d1f0260f0387d54fec4147b10f79b385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{x}\\equiv75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06aa075c15bad739aed0929502a050aa8ded7eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015^{2016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> has an even exponent, we conclude that the last two digits will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee15bcda68b5cfb95764b5cbea63965017b84187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25-17=\\underline{0}8 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"197\" height=\"30\" />.\n~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jDHIJ8o4VSA\">https://youtu.be/jDHIJ8o4VSA</a> (CREATIVE THINKING)\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GVPF6CcCugU\">https://youtu.be/GVPF6CcCugU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p>&#160;<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=2683\">https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=2683</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B\">2016 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_